-- allium: 3
-- Orchestration spec for menu generation state transitions.
-- The umbrella spec (menu-generator.allium) owns entity declarations for
-- Generation, MenuItem, MenuItemRequest, GlobalStatus and CardStatus.
-- This spec adds the orchestration rules that govern:
--   - Parse routing (text vs image)
--   - Fan-out from parsed items to MenuItem entities
--   - Global status reconciliation after each card outcome
--   - Per-card regenerate and inline editing
--   - MenuItem lifecycle invariants

use "./menu-generator.allium" as umbrella
use "./generator-service.allium" as svc

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

-- No module-level given block. Rules are scoped to trigger bindings.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Flow: Parse routing
-- The umbrella's StartGeneration rule transitions Generation to parsing and
-- fires OnGenerateMenu. This rule refines what happens during parsing:
-- the orchestrator dispatches to the appropriate parse operation based on
-- whether a reference photo was supplied.

rule ParseRouting {
    -- After a Generation enters parsing, the orchestrator routes to either
    -- text or image parsing depending on the request content.
    -- If reference_photo is absent, parseMenuFromText is called with the
    -- prompt text. If reference_photo is present, parseMenuFromImage is called
    -- with the image file. Both operations signal completion via
    -- OnParseSucceeded or OnParseFailed (consumed by ParseComplete and
    -- ParseFailed in the umbrella).
    when: OnGenerateMenu(request)
    requires:
        exists umbrella/Generation where global_status = parsing

    @guidance
        -- Implementation: call parseMenuFromText(request.prompt.text, { signal })
        -- when request.reference_photo = null; call
        -- parseMenuFromImage(request.reference_photo.file, { signal }) otherwise.
        -- The AbortSignal is provided by the orchestrator so the active parse
        -- operation is cancelled when a new OnGenerateMenu fires before the
        -- previous one completes. The parse result is delivered via
        -- OnParseSucceeded or OnParseFailed, which the umbrella's ParseComplete
        -- and ParseFailed rules consume.
}

-- Flow: Fan-out from parsed items to MenuItem entities

rule PadOrTrimToCount {
    -- Before fan-out, the raw parser result list is normalised so its length
    -- exactly equals generation.request.count. Two cases:
    --   Trim: if the parser returned more than count items, only the first
    --         count items are kept. The remainder are silently dropped.
    --   Pad:  if the parser returned fewer than count items, blank
    --         ParsedMenuItem records ({category:"", name:"", description:"",
    --         price:""}) are appended until the list length equals count.
    -- After normalisation, FanOutGeneration creates exactly count MenuItem
    -- entities, so generation.items.length = generation.request.count always
    -- holds after OnParseSucceeded completes.
    -- Pad-inserted items are blank (both name and description empty), so they
    -- are created at status=pending and remain there — they are never
    -- automatically advanced to generating. The user must populate at least
    -- one field and click ↻ to start generation for a blank card.
    when: OnParseSucceeded(generation, items: List<svc/ParsedMenuItem>)
    requires: generation.global_status = parsing
    let count = generation.request.count
    let normalised = pad_or_trim(items, count)
    ensures:
        normalised.length = count

    @guidance
        -- pad_or_trim(items, count) is a black box:
        --   if items.length > count → items.take(count)        (trim)
        --   if items.length < count → items + blank_items(count - items.length) (pad)
        --   else                   → items                     (pass-through)
        -- blank_items(n) produces n ParsedMenuItem records with all string
        -- fields set to "".
        -- Implementations must apply PadOrTrimToCount and FanOutGeneration
        -- atomically on the same OnParseSucceeded trigger; the normalised
        -- list is the input to FanOutGeneration's for-loop.
}

rule FanOutGeneration {
    -- After parsing succeeds and the item list has been normalised to
    -- exactly generation.request.count entries (see PadOrTrimToCount), one
    -- MenuItem is created per normalised ParsedMenuItem. Items with a
    -- non-empty name OR non-empty description are created at status=pending
    -- and immediately advance to generating via NonBlankItemStartsGenerating
    -- (umbrella). Items where both name and description are empty are created
    -- at status=pending and stay there until the user fills in at least one
    -- field and clicks regenerate.
    -- Post-condition: generation.items.length = generation.request.count.
    when: OnParseSucceeded(generation, items: List<svc/ParsedMenuItem>)
    requires: generation.global_status = parsing
    ensures:
        for item in items:
            umbrella/MenuItem.created(
                generation: generation,
                category: item.category,
                name: item.name,
                description: item.description,
                price: item.price,
                status: pending
            )

    @guidance
        -- The umbrella's ParseComplete rule transitions generation.global_status
        -- from parsing to generating. FanOutGeneration fires on the same trigger
        -- (OnParseSucceeded) and creates the MenuItem entities. The checker treats
        -- these as separate rules for the same trigger; requires guards must be
        -- non-overlapping. ParseComplete guards on global_status = parsing and
        -- updates the status; FanOutGeneration guards on the same condition and
        -- creates entities. Implementations must apply PadOrTrimToCount,
        -- FanOutGeneration and ParseComplete all atomically.
        -- In practice, implementations pass the normalised list (output of
        -- pad_or_trim) as the `items` argument here, so the for-loop iterates
        -- over exactly generation.request.count elements.
        -- An empty items list with count=0 is valid (the parser found no
        -- structured menu data and none were requested). In that case no MenuItem
        -- entities are created and the generation moves to generating with zero
        -- items. GlobalStatusReconciliation will immediately resolve this as done.
}

-- Flow: Global status reconciliation after each card outcome

rule OnCardSucceeded {
    -- Fired by the image generation service when a dish image has been produced
    -- for a specific card. The card's status and image_url are updated, then
    -- GlobalStatusReconciliation fires to recompute the generation's overall status.
    when: OnDishImageReady(id, blob: svc/ImageBlob)
    let item = umbrella/MenuItem{id: id}
    requires: exists item
    requires: item.status = generating
    ensures:
        item.status = ready
        item.image_url = create_object_url(blob)
        GlobalStatusReconciliation(generation: item.generation)

    @guidance
        -- create_object_url is a black box wrapping URL.createObjectURL.
        -- The resulting URL is a Blob object URL valid for the lifetime of the page.
}

rule OnCardFailed {
    -- Fired by the image generation service when dish image generation failed
    -- for a specific card. The card's status is set to error, then
    -- GlobalStatusReconciliation fires.
    when: OnDishImageFailed(id, error: String)
    let item = umbrella/MenuItem{id: id}
    requires: exists item
    requires: item.status = generating
    ensures:
        item.status = error
        GlobalStatusReconciliation(generation: item.generation)

    @guidance
        -- The error message is available from the GeneratorError delivered by
        -- the generator service (wrapped via wrap_generator_error in
        -- generator-service.allium). The card's errorMessage field is updated
        -- by the implementation for display purposes.
}

rule GlobalStatusReconciliation {
    -- Recomputes generation.global_status after any card outcome. Fires
    -- whenever OnCardSucceeded or OnCardFailed emit a GlobalStatusReconciliation
    -- trigger. The non-blank item set is the set of items where
    -- name != "" or description != "".
    --
    -- Resolution rules (applied in priority order):
    --   no non-blank items                          → done
    --   all non-blank items at error                → error
    --   any non-blank item at generating or pending → generating (still in flight)
    --   some non-blank ready AND some non-blank error → partial
    --   all non-blank items at ready                → done
    when: GlobalStatusReconciliation(generation)
    requires: generation.global_status = generating
    ensures:
        if generation.items.all(i => i.name = "" and i.description = ""):
            generation.global_status = done
        else if generation.items.all(
                i => (i.name = "" and i.description = "") or i.status = error):
            generation.global_status = error
        else if generation.items.any(
                i => (i.name != "" or i.description != "")
                and i.status in {generating, pending}):
            generation.global_status = generating
        else if generation.ready_items.count > 0 and generation.failed_items.count > 0:
            generation.global_status = partial
        else:
            generation.global_status = done

    @guidance
        -- "Non-blank item" means name != "" or description != "". Blank items
        -- (both empty) are excluded from all status counts because they are not
        -- in flight — they are awaiting user input.
        -- The ordering of branches matters: the in-flight check (generating or
        -- pending) must precede the partial check so that a mix of generating +
        -- error cards is reported as still generating, not partial.
}

-- Flow: Per-card regenerate

rule RegenerateSingleCard {
    -- Resets exactly one card back to generating and clears transient fields,
    -- regardless of the card's prior status. Valid prior statuses are:
    --   pending   → generating  (user filled fields and clicked ↻)
    --   generating → generating (no-op on status; image_url cleared and
    --                            generation restarts — guard kept to prevent
    --                            double-fire against an already-in-flight card;
    --                            implementations may choose to ignore this case)
    --   ready     → generating  (user clicks ↻ on a completed card per §1.2 step 5)
    --   error     → generating  (user clicks ↻ to retry a failed card)
    -- Sibling cards are not affected. The generation's global_status moves to
    -- generating because at least one card is now in flight.
    -- Blank items (both name and description empty) have a disabled ↻ trigger
    -- in the UI; this rule therefore only fires for items where
    -- name != "" or description != "".
    when: OnRegenerateCard(id)
    let item = umbrella/MenuItem{id: id}
    requires: exists item
    requires: item.status in {error, pending, ready}
    requires: item.name != "" or item.description != ""
    ensures:
        item.status = generating
        item.image_url = null
        item.generation.global_status = generating

    @guidance
        -- Clearing image_url prevents a stale image from showing while the new
        -- one is being generated. The generation's global_status is forced to
        -- generating unconditionally: since this card is now in flight, the
        -- generation cannot be done or partial.
        -- The blank-item guard (name != "" or description != "") is a
        -- correctness guard, not merely a UX hint. Without it a blank card
        -- could be submitted for generation with no usable prompt. The surface
        -- must disable the ↻ button for blank cards so users never see the
        -- trigger rejected.
        -- The umbrella's RegenerateCard rule covers the same trigger. This rule
        -- adds the widened status guard (error, pending, ready), the blank-item
        -- guard, the image_url clearing, and the global_status side-effect.
        -- Implementations combine both rule bodies atomically.
}

-- Flow: Inline card field editing

rule EditDoesNotChangeStatus {
    -- Updating a card field does not affect that card's status or any sibling
    -- card's status. The generation's global_status is also unaffected.
    when: OnEditCardField(id, field, value)
    let item = umbrella/MenuItem{id: id}
    requires: exists item
    ensures:
        update_card_field(item, field, value)

    @guidance
        -- update_card_field is a black box that sets the named field
        -- (category, name, description, or price) on the targeted card.
        -- Status is not part of the set of editable fields; editing does not
        -- trigger any status transition. If the user wants to regenerate after
        -- editing, they click ↻ (OnRegenerateCard).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant DoneImpliesAllNonBlankReady {
    for g in umbrella/Generations:
        g.global_status = done implies
            g.items.all(i => i.status = ready or (i.name = "" and i.description = ""))
}

invariant PartialImpliesSomeReadyAndSomeFailed {
    for g in umbrella/Generations:
        g.global_status = partial implies
            g.ready_items.count > 0 and g.failed_items.count > 0
}

-- RegenerateDoesNotAffectSiblings: When OnRegenerateCard fires for card C,
-- every sibling card S (same generation, S.id != C.id) retains its status,
-- image_url and all other fields unchanged. This is a temporal ordering
-- property and cannot be expressed as a single-snapshot expression-bearing
-- invariant; it is enforced by the RegenerateSingleCard and
-- EditDoesNotChangeStatus rules, which scope all ensures clauses to the
-- targeted item only.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "FanOutGeneration vs ParseComplete atomicity — both rules fire on OnParseSucceeded with the same guard (generation.global_status = parsing). The umbrella's ParseComplete transitions global_status to generating; FanOutGeneration creates MenuItem entities. The checker may warn about overlapping preconditions. Should these be merged into a single rule in the umbrella, or is the split across files by design?"

open question "GlobalStatusReconciliation trigger — this spec introduces GlobalStatusReconciliation as a chained trigger emitted by OnCardSucceeded and OnCardFailed. The umbrella's AllItemsSucceeded, SomeItemsSucceeded, AllItemsFailed and PartialBecomesComplete rules also reconcile global_status, triggered by Generation.global_status transitions_to generating/partial. Are both reconciliation mechanisms needed, or should the umbrella rules be removed in favour of this explicit trigger?"

open question "OnDishImageReady / OnDishImageFailed surfaces — these triggers are consumed by OnCardSucceeded and OnCardFailed rules here but no surface in the umbrella or generator-service.allium declares them as entry points from the generator service. A surface update to GeneratorServiceCallbacks is needed. Deferred to the task that integrates the generator service callback wiring."

open question "MenuItem entity plural form — the umbrella declares 'Generation.items' as a relationship but the entity collection plural for invariants should be 'umbrella/Generations'. Confirm the checker resolves qualified entity collection names correctly before promotion."
